  "about": "eden:hanoi_board (from #1794). Three rings (small, medium, large), each on peg a, b or c; all start on a. With empty hands ('Put down what you hold before moving the rings.') a Soul moves one ring in two seconds: the ring must be on the peg it names as the source, the destination must be another peg ('Choose a different destination peg.'), no smaller ring may lie on the ring ('A smaller ring lies on top of it') nor on the destination ('A larger ring cannot go on a smaller ring; choose another peg.'). The small ring is always on top, so it names only a destination. Reset puts every ring back on a, refused when they already are ('The same rings are already reset on peg a.').",
